  "overview": {
    "en": "Nikola Tesla was a Serbian-American inventor and electrical engineer who developed the alternating current (AC) electrical system and made pioneering contributions to electromagnetism and wireless communication. His inventions and theoretical work helped shape the modern electrical power industry.",
